  "configuration_id": "config_032",
  "reason": "Evidence: The largest performance jump in the study came from switching singleprofile→multiprofile (config_028: 0.536 → config_030: 0.632, +10 pts), with avgpool aggregation. scvi_n200 consistently outperforms pca_n2000, and concat fusion is the only fusion tested in the multiprofile regime. Uncertainty: We have only tested one aggregation method (avgpool) for multiprofile. It is unclear whether a transformer-based aggregation could capture richer inter-profile interactions and push performance further, or whether avgpool is already near-optimal. What this tests: config_032 is a clean one-variable change from the current best (config_030), replacing avgpool with transformer aggregation while keeping scvi_n200, resnet50, and concat fusion fixed. This isolates the effect of the aggregation mechanism. Why this is the best next experiment: The aggregation method is the dimension most directly responsible for the largest observed gain, so resolving whether transformer aggregation helps (or hurts) relative to avgpool is the highest-information single experiment. It either opens a promising new direction (if transformer >> avgpool) or confirms avgpool sufficiency, allowing budget to be redirected to other axes (e.g., fusion method or image encoder)."
}

